  "query_preview": "..\nA weak line of convergence associated with a broad trough centered\nnear Yap State and easterly trade winds is sitting over the Marianas\nand bringing scattered showers to the region through tomorrow with\nisolated thunderstorms. The risk for isolated thunderstorms will\ncontinue through at least Sunday night as an upper-level trough\nmoves into the region and wind shear increases significantly.\nHowever, a diffusive low-level flow and dry upper level air will \nlikely keep storm coverage isolated. By Monday, the upper level\ntrough will start to move out and only isolated showers are \nanticipated the rest of the forecast period. As winds decrease over\nthe next couple of days, there is a slight chance for island-effect \nshowers Tuesday and Wednesday over Guam.",
